<PageLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How affiliate links are marked on Ruta y Ritmo and what changes for you."
  crumb="Affiliates"
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 20 October 2026.</p>

  <h2>Transparency before the link</h2>
  <p>
    Ruta y Ritmo may include affiliate links in gear or nutrition articles. If you buy
    through one of them, the site may receive a commission. The price you pay is the same
    and the commission does not influence the recommendation.
  </p>

  <h2>How products are chosen</h2>
  <p>
    We only link to products we have used or consider a useful reference for specific
    reasons: durability, price, fit or availability. We do not publish positive reviews
    for money. If content is sponsored, it is marked at the top and is not mixed with an
    independent review.
  </p>

  <h2>What changes for you</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in the price. The shop pays the commission. If you prefer to avoid it, you
    can search for the product directly in the shop; the article will be the same.
  </p>

  <h2>Amazon and other programs</h2>
  <p>
    If Ruta y Ritmo takes part in the Amazon Associates program, the declaration required
    by its terms will be added here. The same applies to any other affiliate program: the
    relationship will be made public before the link appears in an article.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you spot a link that is not marked correctly or a recommendation you do not think
    is honest, email me at{' '}
    <a href="mailto:hola@rutayritmo.com">hola@rutayritmo.com</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
